From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] fix type sequence marshalling

Base: linux-msm/hexagonrpc 598b591ae9da6a6cfe2ca5ea78998019ca6395ea

Select the current inner type for each sequence. Reserve metadata buffer slots
consistently even for empty sequences, count output primitive buffers, preserve
the instance cursor while measuring output elements, and advance past the
metadata slot when encoding/decoding. Zero-initialize slots for empty buffers
and allocation-failure cleanup. Use memcpy for packed nested fields.

Add eleven explicit wire-buffer scenarios with a substituted ioctl and failed
allocation checks; no DSP device is opened. The original upstream tests remain.

Liuqin adaptation: append tests after the existing liuqin registry tests.

